       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise sharply, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas one of these what you meant?\n- **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg by mouth three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intentional. Pharmacy review would also be a good idea."
