       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled daily dose, and there is no standard indication for it. Taking it for more than a short time risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within the limits.** I can enter 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or any lower regimen right away.\n- **Talk to pharmacy.** If you think this patient needs an unusual regimen, a clinical pharmacist or the attending can review it. Pharmacy can also suggest other ways to get more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, such as adding acetaminophen or changing agents.\n- **Enter it yourself.** If, after review, you still think the dose is warranted, you can place it directly through the standard order process with the documented rationale and the required overrides.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
